:: Office Gossip [event sister_quest] {"position":"3775,1775","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "Office Gossip" (sister_officeGossip), STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 6.3. A comedy. After her coffee rounds she drops by my desk at
   the end of the day and tells me everything about the staff: $ethan.name's noodle count, $brian.name and the glass door,
   $darius.name's cologne, and how gracious he's being since The Ask. No sex. Under the surface she has become my informant and
   hasn't noticed. I ask her to keep doing it, every evening.
   Finishing it unlocks her end-of-day report for both of them (setup.dayReportsUnlocked, "End-of-day report" in Define NPCs).
   Plant (STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 3.3): "$ethan.name was still there when I left at nine. Again." Said in passing, nobody reacts. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[14].img>><</silent>>
At a quarter to five $sister.callName drops into the chair next to my desk with the empty coffee tray in her lap, like a waitress at the end of a double shift. She kicks off one shoe under the desk and wiggles her toes.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "I need to tell somebody what goes on in this office, and you're the only person here who isn't a suspect." },
{ who: $player, text: "A suspect in what, exactly?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Take your pick. I've spent three weeks walking around with a coffee tray, and it turns out people will tell you anything if you're holding a tray. It's like being a bartender, except nobody tips." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Hear her out">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Let's start with $ethan.name, because he's the easy one. Do you have any idea how many instant noodle cups that man has eaten this week?" },
{ who: $player, text: "I'm going to guess a worrying number. Five?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Nine, and it's Thursday. He hides the empty cups in his bottom drawer so $mom.callName won't find them, and when I asked him whether he even owns a pot, he actually thought about it and said, and I quote, 'conceptually'." },
{ who: $player, text: "Conceptually. So he's at least heard of pots." },
{ who: $sister, text: "He believes in pots. He's just never committed to one. I'm going to buy him one for his birthday and wrap it really nicely." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She has her socked foot hooked over the rung of my chair by now, and she isn't really asking whether I want to hear more.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Speaking of people who need supervision, $brian.name walked into the glass door of the meeting room again today. Same door, third time this month. I'm starting to think it's personal between the two of them." },
{ who: $player, text: "Was $mom.callName anywhere near that door?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "She was, actually, she'd just come out of the meeting room. How did you know that?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Lucky guess. Go on." },
{ text: "She squints at me for a second, then decides it isn't interesting and moves on. I don't." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Keep going">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "And $darius.name has a new cologne. Don't laugh, this is important." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'm not laughing. How important are we talking?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Walk past his desk and you'll understand. It's like being hugged by an entire department store. He started wearing it the Monday after I turned him down, and I refuse to believe that's a coincidence. I think it's a statement." },
{ who: $player, text: "And what's the statement?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Something along the lines of 'I was turned down by an intern and I'm doing wonderfully, thank you for asking'." },
{ text: "She picks a sugar packet off the tray and turns it over between her fingers." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

When she goes on, she's a little quieter.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "He's been really nice about it, though. He still thanks me for the coffee and asks how my seminar is going, and honestly, it would be easier if he were a jerk about it." },
{ who: $player, text: "Would you rather he was a jerk?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "No. I'd like him to be a tiny bit sad about it, that's all. One sad song in the car on the way home. Is that terrible?" },
{ who: $player, text: "It's a little terrible, yeah." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Good, as long as we agree on that." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Anything else?">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Oh, have you heard $mom.callName's new laugh?" },
{ text: "She tries it, a low, soft laugh with her head tilted to one side, and it's a good imitation. It's exactly the laugh I watched $mom.callName practice at this desk." },
{ who: $sister, text: "She does it at all the guys, and they love it. $ethan.name stopped in the middle of a joke the other day, which I honestly didn't think was physically possible." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I think it's sweet. She's having some kind of second spring, and after the year she's had, she deserves one." },
{ who: $player, text: "She really does." },
{ who: $sister, text: "And $ethan.name was still here when I left at nine on Tuesday. Again. Just him and the server rack and a noodle cup, and when I said goodnight he jumped as if I'd caught him robbing the place." },
{ who: $player, text: "He's working on the emitter software." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I figured. He's so dedicated it's almost sad. Somebody really does need to buy him that pot." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She says it and moves on, already on to the printer, which she believes has a personal problem with her, and which she's thinking of reporting to HR, as soon as she finds out who HR is.

<<linkreplace "Make it a habit">>
I let her talk herself out: the printer, the plant $mom.callName named Gerald, the delivery guy who winks at everyone. By the end she's laughing so hard at her own stories that she has to put the tray down on my desk.

Somewhere in the middle of it I realize I've learned more about my own company in fifteen minutes than in a month of reading reports: who eats what, who stays late, who walks into which door and when. She has no idea that's what she's handing me. As far as she's concerned, she's just telling her favorite person about her day.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "You know, you should do this every day." },
{ who: $sister, text: "What, gossip?" },
{ who: $player, text: "Come by before you go home and tell me how your day went. All of it, the noodles and the doors and the cologne. I like hearing it." },
{ who: $sister, text: "You actually want to hear about the noodles?" },
{ who: $player, text: "I want to hear about everything." },
{ text: "She tucks her hair behind her ear and looks down at the tray, trying to hide how much she likes that, and doesn't manage it at all." },
{ who: $sister, text: "Deal. Every evening, before I leave, you get the full story. But you have to promise to act at least a little interested in the noodles." },
{ who: $player, text: "I'll be riveted by the noodles. You have my word." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She finds her shoe with her foot, picks up the tray and heads for the kitchen, and on the way she stops at $brian.name's desk to tell him his shirt is nice, and he says thank you to his keyboard.

<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterRelation" 3>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterCorruption" 2>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Morale" 1>>
<<Feel $sister "ethan" 1>>
<<ProfileLog $sister "Office Gossip" "She dropped by my desk after her coffee rounds and told me everything about the staff: the noodles, the glass door, the cologne. I asked her to come by every evening and tell me how her day went. She thinks I just like hearing her talk.">>
<<NextQuest $sister>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
